                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237394658",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198394056856",
                            "num_reviews": 2,
                            "playtime_forever": 46388,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 46388,
                            "last_played": 1781020131
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "**The perfect game for a geek like me.**\n\nI don't think I've ever played a game that fits my brain this well. I'm the kind of person who can get lost in figuring out how things work, why they work, and how to make them work better. Oxygen Not Included takes that part of me and turns it into hundreds of hours of pure enjoyment.\n\nThere's something incredibly satisfying about starting with an absolute mess, slowly understanding the systems behind it, and eventually building something that actually works. And then, of course, realizing there's a better way to do it and spending another three hours rebuilding the whole damn thing.\n\nI love how the game rewards curiosity and patience instead of simply handing me answers. I can spend an unreasonable amount of time thinking about heat, gas flow, power efficiency, or some ridiculously complicated automation setup, and somehow never get bored. Even my failures are fun because there's always something new to learn from them.\n\nWhat really gets me is that the more I understand this game, the more I appreciate just how much depth it has. There are so many little details and interconnected systems that make me feel like I'm constantly discovering something new. It's one of those rare games that makes me feel genuinely smart when things work out and humbly reminds me that I'm an idiot when they don't.\n\nI can confidently say this game was made for people like me. People who enjoy overthinking things, solving problems nobody asked them to solve, and finding satisfaction in making complicated systems work just a little bit better.\n\n**I don't just enjoy playing Oxygen Not Included. I enjoy the way it makes me think.** And honestly, finding a game that clicks with your brain on this level is a special feeling.\n\nAn easy 10/10 for me. I could spend hundreds more hours on this game and still have a dozen new ideas to try. Absolutely love it.",
